  "lineage": "Corsican three-voice unaccompanied sacred-and-secular polyphonic tradition — the canonical Corsican vocal-polyphonic form built on three named voice-parts (secondu the lead text-carrying voice, bassu the bass-anchor voice, terzu the highest-and-most-ornamented voice that enters last), performed in stone-walled village-church contexts and in lay confraternity (cunfraterne) sacred-paraliturgical contexts, with the canonical regional centers in Niolu, Castagniccia, Sartène-Tallano, Balagne; the modern revival from the 1970s-onward through riacquistu Corsican cultural-resurgence groups Canta u Populu Corsu, A Filetta, Tavagna, I Muvrini, and the contemporary ethnomusicology lineage of Bernard Lortat-Jacob and Jean-Étienne Antonini",
